Hi,

I'm attempting to filter my SNP dataset, which is a gl object, using the gl.filter.maf function.

/// GENLIGHT OBJECT /////////

 // 43 genotypes,  40,764 binary SNPs, size: 5.7 Mb
 497318 (28.37 %) missing data

 // Basic content
   @gen: list of 43 SNPbin

 // Optional content
   @ind.names:  43 individual labels
   @loc.names:  40764 locus labels
   @chromosome: factor storing chromosomes of the SNPs
   @position: integer storing positions of the SNPs
   @pop: population of each individual (group size range: 5-19)
   @other: a list containing: elements without names

I'm getting the following error:

Error in if (nLoc(x) != nrow(x@other$loc.metrics)) { :
  argument is of length zero

I also get this error when I try to do the gl.report.maf, but I don't have any trouble filtering using any of the other filtering functions. Can you please let me know what I may be doing wrong? Please let me know what other information you would need to answer my question. The files are too large to attach, but I can provide them with another means if necessary.

Thanks!

