This creates the names of locis above the threshold (in any pair) and finally to filter your genlight object

!(locNames(possums.gl <http://possums.gl>) %in% locisout)   #an index which loci should be not used (out=TRUE)

poss.filld <- possums.gl <http://possums.gl>[, !(locNames(possums.gl <http://possums.gl>) %in% locisout)]

This filters the loci (and leaves the one in which are below the threshold all the time over all pairs)

Do not forget to update also the meta data via:

poss.filld@other$loc.metrics <- poss.filld@other$loc.metrics[!(locNames(possums.gl <http://possums.gl>) %in% locisout),]

[possums.gl <http://possums.gl> does not have one, but your data set has most often metadata ]

Hope that helps,

Bernd

